WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:01.422
With just a fraction of

00:00:01.856 --> 00:00:03.324
humanitarian aid reaching those

00:00:03.858 --> 00:00:08.196
whose lives depended on.

00:00:08.463 --> 00:00:10.331
&gt;&gt; Fresh snow blanketed the

00:00:10.598 --> 00:00:12.366
hills of the province in

00:00:12.633 --> 00:00:13.167
central Afghanistan.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:14.402
Creating the illusion of a

00:00:14.669 --> 00:00:15.403
winter wonderland.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.339
But, for those who live here,

00:00:18.606 --> 00:00:19.474
there is no wonder.

00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:21.509
Let alone a glimmer of hope.

00:00:22.176 --> 00:00:24.278
Simply staying alive is a

00:00:24.545 --> 00:00:25.313
deadly struggle.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.249
For this family, their young

00:00:28.516 --> 00:00:29.517
son lost that battle.

00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:32.253
Now, they huddle around his

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.389
hillside grave, offering

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:36.357
prayers to six year old what

00:00:36.624 --> 00:00:37.425
he'd who, just days ago, froze

00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:38.292
to death.

00:00:39.127 --> 00:00:41.295
&gt;&gt; I miss my brother, and that

00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:43.231
is why I came to visit him at

00:00:43.498 --> 00:00:44.265
the graveyard he says.

00:00:44.532 --> 00:00:47.301
&gt;&gt; Abdul moved his family to

00:00:47.568 --> 00:00:49.904
the township in core --

00:00:50.171 --> 00:00:51.339
looking for work as a labor.

00:00:53.141 --> 00:00:54.208
Taliban-controlled Afghanistan,

00:00:54.475 --> 00:00:57.445
he was unable to make ends

00:00:57.912 --> 00:00:58.179
meet.

00:00:58.446 --> 00:00:58.813
[Speaking non-english]

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.448
I had nothing to bring to keep

00:01:00.715 --> 00:01:02.250
the house warm, he explains, I

00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:03.351
checked on the children during

00:01:03.918 --> 00:01:04.485
the night and their bodies were

00:01:04.752 --> 00:01:04.852
numb.

00:01:05.186 --> 00:01:08.422
I realized my son had died.

00:01:09.157 --> 00:01:11.325
&gt;&gt; This is a photo of him last

00:01:11.592 --> 00:01:13.261
year, he says.

00:01:13.528 --> 00:01:16.230
And this is his dead body.

00:01:16.497 --> 00:01:18.699
And president sly brutal winter

00:01:18.966 --> 00:01:20.268
has claimed countless Afghan

00:01:20.535 --> 00:01:21.402
lives this year.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.471
But so too has extreme poverty.

00:01:24.172 --> 00:01:25.439
This has been exacerbated by

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.175
the repercussions of the

00:01:27.441 --> 00:01:28.376
Taliban governments dystopian

00:01:28.643 --> 00:01:30.311
gender policies.

00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:31.445
♪ ♪ ♪

00:01:31.946 --> 00:01:33.214
and the response by the

00:01:33.481 --> 00:01:34.382
international communities.

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:36.350
Almost a year ago, the Taliban

00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:38.152
banned female secondary school

00:01:38.419 --> 00:01:40.254
students from attending school,

00:01:40.521 --> 00:01:41.322
that has morphed into a

00:01:41.589 --> 00:01:43.291
nationwide event on all female

00:01:43.558 --> 00:01:44.225
education.

00:01:44.492 --> 00:01:46.194
But, it was the Taliban's

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.229
decision in December, banning

00:01:48.496 --> 00:01:49.330
women from working for non

00:01:49.597 --> 00:01:51.265
governmental organizations that

00:01:51.532 --> 00:01:53.134
forced humanitarian aid groups

00:01:53.401 --> 00:01:55.336
to abruptly halt or suspend

00:01:55.603 --> 00:01:55.970
operations.

00:01:56.137 --> 00:02:00.541
&gt;&gt; There is 28 million Afghans

00:02:00.808 --> 00:02:02.243
in desperate need at the

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:02.643
moment.

00:02:04.178 --> 00:02:04.378
28 million.

00:02:04.645 --> 00:02:06.280
And we're not even reaching a

00:02:06.547 --> 00:02:07.281
fraction of those.

00:02:07.548 --> 00:02:09.317
&gt;&gt; The Norwegian refugee

00:02:09.584 --> 00:02:10.418
council says, they normally

00:02:10.685 --> 00:02:13.187
helped 700,000 Afghans each

00:02:13.454 --> 00:02:13.588
year's.

00:02:14.155 --> 00:02:15.256
But the operation has been

00:02:15.523 --> 00:02:16.290
drastically --

00:02:16.557 --> 00:02:18.326
the secretary general, recently

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:21.195
traveled to kabul, pleading the

00:02:21.462 --> 00:02:22.363
collab and to allow female aid

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:23.564
workers to return to work.

00:02:24.165 --> 00:02:25.399
&gt;&gt; It is at its worst hour.

00:02:25.666 --> 00:02:28.202
It's never been as bad as it is

00:02:28.469 --> 00:02:28.536
now.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:32.273
&gt;&gt; 35-year-old --

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.208
wipes away her tears as she

00:02:34.475 --> 00:02:35.376
grieves for her husband who

00:02:35.643 --> 00:02:38.179
perished from the cold also in

00:02:38.446 --> 00:02:38.479
--

00:02:38.746 --> 00:02:40.248
province, father and

00:02:40.514 --> 00:02:41.315
breadwinner for their eight

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:42.416
children, the youngest of just

00:02:42.683 --> 00:02:42.750
two.

00:02:43.184 --> 00:02:45.186
Now, she's wondering how to

00:02:45.453 --> 00:02:46.320
keep her family alive.

00:02:48.155 --> 00:02:48.522
[Speaking non-english]

00:02:49.156 --> 00:02:51.225
&gt;&gt; I have no education, she

00:02:51.492 --> 00:02:51.592
says.

00:02:52.026 --> 00:02:52.593
My children need food, what

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.227
should I do?

00:02:55.162 --> 00:02:58.165
Three of her children are girls,

00:02:58.432 --> 00:02:58.833
including 12-year-old --

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.269
who knows all too well what

00:03:01.535 --> 00:03:03.204
happens to poor young Afghan

00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:05.339
girls who reach puberty.

00:03:06.207 --> 00:03:06.574
[Speaking non-english]

00:03:06.841 --> 00:03:07.475
&gt;&gt; I am worried that if we

00:03:08.175 --> 00:03:09.343
don't have food, my brothers

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.312
will be forced to sell or marry

00:03:11.579 --> 00:03:12.346
me under pressure, she says.

00:03:13.147 --> 00:03:14.315
I don't want to get married.

00:03:14.582 --> 00:03:14.749
I'm a kid.

00:03:15.149 --> 00:03:16.450
I don't want a husband.

00:03:17.151 --> 00:03:19.253
U.S. Charity too young to web

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.188
said they've been able to

00:03:21.455 --> 00:03:22.390
provide emergency aid for the

00:03:22.657 --> 00:03:23.457
family and many others.

00:03:24.158 --> 00:03:27.161
But founder, Stephanie Sinclair,

00:03:27.428 --> 00:03:29.196
says the avalanche of need is

00:03:29.463 --> 00:03:29.697
overwhelming.

00:03:30.164 --> 00:03:31.265
And they're unable to help

00:03:31.532 --> 00:03:31.699
everyone.

00:03:32.066 --> 00:03:33.434
&gt;&gt; To me, it's unconscionable

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:34.435
that the international

00:03:34.702 --> 00:03:36.170
community is not paying more

00:03:36.437 --> 00:03:37.371
attention to what's happening

00:03:37.638 --> 00:03:38.306
to women and girls in

00:03:38.572 --> 00:03:38.773
Afghanistan.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.374
It is simply, just inexcusable

00:03:40.641 --> 00:03:41.309
that we are not doing

00:03:41.575 --> 00:03:43.277
everything in our power to try

00:03:43.544 --> 00:03:45.146
to change the course of what's

00:03:45.413 --> 00:03:45.680
happening there.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:46.580
We have to do better.

00:03:47.148 --> 00:03:48.382
&gt;&gt; And with the U.N. Predicting

00:03:48.649 --> 00:03:49.350
two thirds of the population

